### Why
- **Roth IRA first (tax-free compounding):** Your Roth IRA (••0216) holds 601.434752 uncapped NVDA shares ($30.99 cost basis) and has `option_level_2`. Selling 3 contracts there generates $819 totally tax-free, and any upside assignment wouldn't trigger a capital gains tax bill.
- **Zero earnings gap risk:** NVDA reports Q3 FY27 earnings on **2026-11-17 (after close, verified)**. The **2026-11-13** expiration (26 DTE) is the only chain in the 25–45 day window that expires cleanly before the report, harvesting peak theta decay (-$0.126/day per contract) without binary earnings exposure.
- **Strict ≤50% lot coverage:** Capping 300/601.43 shares in the Roth (49.88%) and 200/452.03 shares in the Individual account (44.24%) leaves over half your shares in each account completely uncapped if NVDA rallies ahead of earnings.

